## 13. `EDGE_CASES.md` — every case considered

| # | Case | Handling |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Repo has no `capability.yaml` | Collector emits `NO_CAPABILITY_YAML` warning; registry still emitted. CI warns, does not block. |
| 2 | Two repos declare `role: seed-expression` | Collector refuses to emit a seed; `MULTIPLE_SEEDS` warning. Resolver refuses to run without a seed. |
| 3 | Two current capabilities share an `id` | Collector emits `AMBIGUOUS_CURRENT`. Resolver returns `CAPABILITY_AMBIGUOUS`. Order fails unless `optional: true`. |
| 4 | Capability is only `incubating` | Resolver returns `DEPRECATED_ONLY`/`CAPABILITY_NOT_FOUND` unless `allow_incubating: true` on the request. Never granted by default. |
| 5 | Capability is only `deprecated` | Resolver returns `DEPRECATED_ONLY`. Order fails unless optional. |
| 6 | Requested `mode` differs from the current branch | `MODE_MISMATCH`. Resolver does not silently substitute. |
| 7 | Branch has no `grade` | Collector emits `UNGRADED_BRANCH`; resolver refuses the capability with `UNGRADED`. |
| 8 | Corporate order requests a `tenant_isolated: false` capability | `TENANT_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION`. Hard fail. |
| 9 | Personal order requests any capability | Personal orders can use non-isolated capabilities; the boundary is one-way. |
| 10 | `capability.yaml` fails schema | Collector skips that repo with `SCHEMA:` warning; other repos still processed. |
| 11 | `capability.yaml` YAML is malformed | `YAML_PARSE_ERROR`; skipped; other repos processed. |
| 12 | `repo.name` in yaml ≠ directory name | `NAME_MISMATCH`; skipped. Prevents accidental forks poisoning the registry. |
| 13 | Registry has no seed | Resolver refuses to run; exits 1. |
| 14 | Order `order_id` is not a ULID | Order schema rejects before resolution. |
| 15 | `tenant_id` is neither `ten_` nor `per_` | Order schema rejects. |
| 16 | Capability id has uppercase or underscores | Contract schema rejects. IDs are lowercase-dash only. |
| 17 | GitHub API rate-limited during discovery | Collector falls back to sibling-directory scan; if empty, emits empty registry with warnings. |
| 18 | Repo archived / private | `gh repo clone` fails per-repo; skipped with a log line; does not block the run. |
| 19 | Two repos both emit a `branch` with the same name | Allowed — branches are namespaced by repo. Capabilities are what collide, not branches. |
| 20 | A branch flips to `deprecated` and back to `current` | Collector records the shed on the first transition; a re-birth is a new `since` date and a new ledger entry. Not silently ignored. |
| 21 | Registry grows too large for one commit | Registry is capped by repo count (65 today); at 500+ repos, shard by `class` or `repo`. The collector already emits deterministic order, so sharding is a pure split. |
| 22 | Two collectors run concurrently | Last writer wins on `registry.json`; both append to `sheds.ndjson` — the ledger is NDJSON, so append is atomic on POSIX for lines under PIPE_BUF. |
| 23 | Resolver called with a stale registry | Every resolution records `resolved_at` and the registry's `generated_at` should be validated externally. Add `--max-age-minutes` if you need hard freshness. |
| 24 | Order references a capability that was `current` at build time, `deprecated` at run time | Resolver returns `DEPRECATED_ONLY`; the caller should re-order or fall back. This is the intended behaviour — the ID never silently rots. |
| 25 | Personal and corporate orders want the same capability | Same resolver path; only the tenant check differs. No forked logic, no fork in the moat. |
| 26 | Free-tier quota exhausted mid-run | Collector writes a partial registry with warnings; the next scheduled run supersedes it. Ledger is append-only, so no shed is lost. |
| 27 | Schema evolves to `v2` | `schema` field is a const; a v2 file is rejected by v1 validators. Migration is a deliberate commit, never silent. |
| 28 | A `capability.yaml` declares a `branch` with no capabilities | Allowed. Branches are containers; capabilities are leaves. This lets you register a branch before its first leaf. |
| 29 | A capability is `produces_again: true` but the branch has no `order-in` node | Collector warns `PRODUCES_AGAIN_NO_ORDER_IN`. Soft warning, not a hard fail — the check is heuristic. |
| 30 | `supersedes` references a repo:branch that does not exist | Collector does not resolve `supersedes`; it is a hint. The ledger is the source of truth for what was actually shed. |

