## 10. `EDGE_CASES.md` — the pipeline

| # | Case | Handling |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Patch manifest missing fields | Schema validator rejects; classify skips the file with a stderr line; other patches still processed. |
| 2 | Corpus blob missing for a `corpus_ref` | `hydrate_payload` raises; rehydrate returns `aborted` with step detail; ledger records it. |
| 3 | Corpus blob hash ≠ `corpus_ref` after hydrate | Rehydrate fails fast with "hash mismatch"; no partial apply. |
| 4 | Two patches cover the same target | Classify marks all but the latest-captured as `superseded`; only the latest reaches rehydration. |
| 5 | Patch targets a repo not checked out | Rehydrate aborts at apply step with `repo not checked out`. |
| 6 | Patch requires a capability that is now `deprecated` | Resolve step fails; rehydrate returns `aborted`; the patch is not shed (it is not the patch's fault). |
| 7 | Patch requires a capability that is `tenant_isolated: false` but tenant is corporate | Resolve fails at tenant boundary; rehydrate aborts; ledger records. |
| 8 | Grade gate times out | Rehydrate returns `shed` with "gate timed out"; the patch is retired, not retried. |
| 9 | Grade gate returns non-zero | Rehydrate returns `shed`; the patch loses to the grade. |
| 10 | Apply succeeds but commit-back fails | Rehydrate returns `aborted` (not `applied`); the working copy is discarded; the ledger records the failure so the patch can be retried safely. |
| 11 | Order/resolution `order_id` mismatch | `idp-execute` refuses; exit 1. |
| 12 | Resolution has non-optional unresolved capabilities | `idp-execute` refuses before building the DAG; exit 1. |
| 13 | agent-foundry not importable | `idp-execute` runs in dry-run mode; outcome `partial` (or `ok` if `--dry-run`); never silently no-ops. |
| 14 | DAG empty (no resolved capabilities) | `build_dag` returns `{"nodes": [], "edges": []}`; execute still emits a valid execution record with `task_executions: 0`. |
| 15 | Two rehydrations touch the same repo concurrently | Rehydrate works in a tempdir, copies back at commit; last writer wins. A future `--lock` flag can serialise; until then, run the batch serially. |
| 16 | Corpus blob is enormous (> RAM) | `sha256_file` streams in 1MB chunks; `hydrate_payload` uses `read_bytes()` — for > 100MB blobs, switch to `shutil.copyfileobj` at the call site. |
| 17 | Patch classification is `unknown` | Classify emits `unknown` with reason; rehydrate is not called for unknown patches; a human reviews the classification file. |
| 18 | A patch was already `applied` in a prior run | Rehydrate does not check state — the caller (workflow or batch script) filters. The ledger is the source of truth for what was applied. |
| 19 | Repository is a shallow clone | Apply can still copy; grade gates that need history will fail; the ledger records the failure. CI clones with `fetch-depth: 0`. |
| 20 | Two different tenants issue the same order | Both resolve independently; the DAGs are identical; the meter records per-tenant. No cross-tenant memory. |
| 21 | Ledger file grows unbounded | NDJSON append-only; rotate monthly by date. The ledger is the audit trail — never rewrite it. |
| 22 | Classify finds zero patches | Exits 1 with "no patches found"; the workflow stops before rehydration. |
| 23 | Rehydrate finds the patch but the repo dir exists but is empty | Apply succeeds (creates the file); grade gate decides. |
| 24 | `corpus_ref` uses a hash algorithm other than sha256 | Schema rejects at manifest level. Only sha256 is accepted in v1. |
| 25 | agent-foundry raises during run | `run_dag` catches, returns `outcome: "failed"` with stderr line; the execution record is still written. |
| 26 | Order has one capability, resolution has zero resolved | `build_dag` returns empty DAG; execute returns `partial`; the caller sees the mismatch in the ledger. |
| 27 | Two patches target the same file in the same repo | The batch applies them serially; the second patch sees the first patch's output; if the grade fails, only the second is shed. |
| 28 | Corpus directory is on a network filesystem (slow) | `hydrate_payload` uses local tempdir; the copy is one-shot; if the network fails mid-copy, the hash check catches it. |
| 29 | Patch `size_bytes` disagrees with actual blob size | Rehydrate does not trust `size_bytes` — it trusts `sha256`. The size is metadata for the manifest, not a gate. |
| 30 | Order references a capability id that exists in the registry but was added after the order was placed | Resolver runs at execution time, so the latest-current binding wins. This is the intended behaviour of late binding. |

